WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.495
Show them, right in the thread. This is photos in chat.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.424
In the composer, choose Photo, then pick one on your device, or take one.

00:00:12.624 --> 00:00:16.798
It waits above the message field, with Remove photo, until you send it.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.214
Send it with text, or without. In the thread, a photo is at most sixteen rem wide,

00:00:25.214 --> 00:00:28.121
at four by three, with any text under it.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.522
A file over ten megabytes is refused, and says why: This file is fourteen megabytes.

00:00:37.522 --> 00:00:39.400
Photos can be up to ten.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:45.363
So is one that isn't a JPEG, PNG, WebP or HEIC photo. Dismiss puts it away.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.889
And a photo someone else sends arrives as it's sent. Here is Walt's, with no reload.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.580
Choose a photo, and it opens full screen.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:03.998
Sent in Everyone, it is in Photos too, under the sender's name. From ten twenty-four

00:01:03.998 --> 00:01:06.783
pixels, a side panel says who, and when.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.876
In a direct message, it works the same way, but it stays between the two of you: not

00:01:14.876 --> 00:01:17.498
in Photos, and only you two can open it.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.337
On a phone, the thread fills the screen.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.830
As it grows, the rail, the conversations and who is here now open beside it.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.151
Once the Popkin wraps up, its photos stay, and still open. There is no Photo to send

00:01:37.151 --> 00:01:37.942
another.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.110
What no screen shows: location and device data are removed before a photo is stored,

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.782
and its address is signed, and expires.

00:01:47.982 --> 00:01:52.458
The server checks the file's own bytes, whatever its name says. And once a photo is

00:01:52.458 --> 00:01:55.454
up, a message tried again doesn't upload it twice.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.764
That is journey thirteen. Popkin is a free platform for pop-up communities.
